---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: `About ${SITE.name}`,
    url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: SITE.author,
      jobTitle: 'Founder and Editor',
      url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
    },
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`Who runs ${SITE.name}, how the guides get written, and why you can trust the picks. Independent reviews with no sponsored placements.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>

      <p class="muted" style="font-size:1.08rem;">
        {SITE.name} is an independent site about the products that make a home work better.
        No sponsored placements, no pay-to-rank, no filler.
      </p>

      <h2>Who writes this</h2>
      <p>
        Hi, I am {SITE.author}. I have spent the last several years working in search and
        content, and a good chunk of that time inside the smart home space specifically,
        writing about connectivity hardware and IoT devices for a US brand. That work meant
        reading a lot of spec sheets, a lot of support tickets, and a lot of one-star reviews.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is where this site came from. Most product roundups are assembled by someone who
        has never touched the thing they are ranking. You can tell, because the guide never
        mentions the annoying detail you only find out in week three. I would rather write the
        version that does.
      </p>

      <h2>What you will find here</h2>
      <p>
        Buying guides and comparisons across five areas: smart home, kitchen and dining,
        home and living, patio and garden, and tools and home improvement. Every guide is
        built to answer one question honestly: which of these should you actually buy, and
        who should skip it.
      </p>

      <h2>How this site makes money</h2>
      <p>
        Through affiliate links, mainly Amazon. If you buy something after clicking one, I earn
        a small commission and you pay exactly the same price. That is the entire business model.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nobody pays for a placement here and no brand gets to review a draft before it goes live.
        If a product is the best one for the job, it gets the top spot. If the budget option is
        good enough for most people, the guide says so, even though the expensive one would pay
        more. You can read the full <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and
        the <a href="/editorial-policy/">testing and editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Products change, prices move, and sometimes I get something wrong. If you spot an error
        or a recommendation that has aged badly, <a href="/contact/">tell me</a> and I will fix
        the page and note the update date.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
